[
{ type: [install, upgrade]
  message: <<EOM
%%PKGNAME%% has been installed into:

    %%WWWDIR%%

Configure %%WWWDIR%%/.env before serving the application. Set LDAP_HOST,
LDAP_USERNAME and LDAP_PASSWORD for your LDAP server, and APP_URL to the
external URL. PHP configuration files are in %%WWWDIR%%/config/.
Local changes to .env and config/*.php are preserved on package upgrades;
compare them with the supplied .example and .sample files after upgrading.

For a NEW installation only, generate the application encryption key as root:

    cd %%WWWDIR%%
    %%LOCALBASE%%/bin/php artisan key:generate --force

Keep the existing APP_KEY when upgrading. If LDAP_PASSWORD_ENC=true is used,
the encrypted LDAP password also depends on that key.

Point your web server at %%WWWDIR%%/public/ and route requests for nonexistent
files to public/index.php. For Apache 2.4 with PHP configured and mod_rewrite
enabled, an example restricted to local access is:

    Alias /phpldapadmin "%%WWWDIR%%/public"
    <Directory "%%WWWDIR%%/public">
        DirectoryIndex index.php
        Options FollowSymLinks
        AllowOverride FileInfo Options
        Require local
    </Directory>

Adjust access restrictions for your site. The PHP worker must run as
%%WWWOWN%%:%%WWWGRP%%, or have equivalent access to storage/ and bootstrap/cache/.
Only these runtime directories need web-server write access.

Put custom JSON templates in %%WWWDIR%%/templates/custom/.

After an upgrade, clear cached configuration and views as the PHP worker:

    cd %%WWWDIR%%
    su -m %%WWWOWN%% -c '%%LOCALBASE%%/bin/php artisan optimize:clear'

Upgrading from version 1 requires manual configuration and template migration:
https://github.com/leenooks/phpLDAPadmin/wiki/Installation-Instructions
EOM
}
]
